#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:9
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:12
msgid "The `test` task provides a means for compiling and running the tests."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:14
msgid "By default, the `test` task in sbt 2.x:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:16
msgid ""
"**Subproject parallelism**. Performs compilation of the relevant subprojects "
"in parallel, specified by the [query](../concepts/sbt-query.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:17
msgid ""
"**Test suite parallelism**. Maps discovered test suites, to tasks and "
"executes them in parallel."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:18
msgid ""
"**Incremental test**. Runs only the tests that either failed in the previous "
"run, never run, or if sbt detects changes in the test or its dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:19
msgid ""
"**Cached**. The test result is cached machine-wide, and optionally remote "
"cached."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:21
msgid "The standard source locations for testing are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:23
msgid "Scala sources in `src/test/scala/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:24
msgid "Java sources in `src/test/java/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:25
msgid "Resources for the test classpath in `src/test/resources/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:27
msgid ""
"The resources may be accessed from tests by using the `getResource` methods "
"of `java.lang.Class` or `java.lang.ClassLoader`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:30
msgid "Test interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:32
msgid ""
"sbt defines the common interface for JVM-based test frameworks, allowing "
"automatic test suite discovery and parallel execution. By default sbt "
"integrates with [MUnit](https://scalameta.org/munit/), [ScalaTest](https://"
"www.scalatest.org/), [Hedgehog](https://hedgehogqa.github.io/scala-"
"hedgehog/), [ScalaCheck](https://scalacheck.org/), [Specs2](https://"
"etorreborre.github.io/specs2/), [Weaver](https://typelevel.org/weaver-"
"test/), [ZIO Test](https://zio.dev/reference/test/), and [JUnit 4](https://"
"github.com/sbt/junit-interface); this means you only need to add the test "
"framework to the classpath to work with sbt. For example, MUnit may be used "
"by declaring it as a `libraryDependency`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:35
msgid "\"org.scalameta\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:35
msgid "\"munit\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:35
msgid "\"1.2.0\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:40
msgid ""
"In the above, `Test` denotes the `Test` configuration, and means that MUnit "
"will only be on the test classpath and it isn't needed by the main sources."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:43
msgid "JUnit"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-test.md:45
msgid ""
"Support for JUnit 5 is provided by [sbt-jupiter-interface](https://"
"github.com/sbt/sbt-jupiter-interface). To add JUnit Jupiter support into "
"your project, add the jupiter-interface dependency in your project's main "
"build.sbt file."
msgstr ""

